{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>From the wilderness of Kedemot.</b> Of the root קדמה, eastward — from the wilderness that is in the east, not from the wilderness that is in the south. And so we find in the book of Judges that there was a wilderness in the east, as it is written: ״ויירשו את כל גבול האמורי מארנון ועד היבוק ומן המדבר ועד הירדן״." "<b>Words of peace.</b> Since most of the land of Sihon was from the land of Moab and Ammon, and not from the land of Canaan, he called to him in peace. But Og, whose land was from the land of the Rephaim, which was from the land of Canaan — he did not call to him in peace, for one does not call to peace over the land of the seven nations, as is explained in the section of Judges."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:26.395663058Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}